syslinuxos-wifi-analyzer (2026.11.1) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * Decode non-ASCII SSIDs as iw escapes them, and treat an all-zero SSID as
    hidden, so names such as "Caffè" display and filter correctly.
  * Show the helper's own error instead of a generic authorization message,
    distinguish a cancelled authorization from a missing polkit agent, and let
    Stop cancel a pending authorization dialog.
  * Closing the window no longer freezes it while a scan finishes; the adapter
    list is read in the background and a missing iw is reported as such.
  * Update the network table in place, keeping the selected cell, scroll
    position and sort order; a radio that changes channel replaces its old row.
  * Add a scan-in-progress indicator and announce errors to assistive
    technology; give the signal graphs a text description and keyboard focus.
  * Fix the clashing keyboard shortcuts in English, Italian, French and German.
  * Make the history graph scroll with time and follow the chosen sensitivity,
    scale the gauge with the system font, and mute beeps at volume zero.
  * Use the theme's colours for titles and stale rows.
  * Limit a scan to the 500 strongest radios and the amount of text read from
    iw, give up after ten consecutive scan errors, scan all channels about once
    a second, and ignore malformed deeply nested commands.
  * Label OWE, WPA3 and WPA2 networks precisely, show 6 GHz channels as such
    and include the 4.9 GHz band.
  * Remove bytecode left by the privileged helper when the package is removed.
  * Singular status line for a single radio; the manual page names the English
    controls.

